Z||000000||fropuff||01-19-2001||10:52 PM||||Hey, I was wondering if anyone has a picture of an automatic shifter knob in a Fiero.  The one I'm looking for is the one that has the square button on top.  I sat in a '01 Corvette, and noticed how cool the knob is.  I think these are also found on the Camaros.  I thought I saw one before, but I can't remember where.  If you have one, I was also wondering if you need to change anything.  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||01-20-2001||12:05 AM||||Most of the GM knobs that I have seen are interchangable. Go to a scrap yard and see if there's one you like. pull the clip out the front and that's it. take it home and swap them over. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||01-20-2001||12:17 AM||||That's good.  I thought I heard that somewhere, but I had to make sure.  It was probably from you.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Anyway, I still kind of want to see a picture of one.  Anyone know what other cars have these knobs on them?  I most likely won't find a 'Vette or Camaro around here.  Thanks again.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||01-20-2001||12:53 PM||||I also forgot to say that with the smaller knob, I want to shorten the shifter a bit.  I know the shifter boot is a problem with a shorter shifter, but will a 1" chop affect it that much?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
