Z||000005||fropuff||01-20-2001||09:51 PM||||Actually, I was thinking of shortening it myself.  I need to save a little for my nitrous.  I might use either a hack saw or a Dremel with a cutoff wheel.  I might just cut a little off at a time.  I would also have to trahsfer the little slot that the U-shaped pin goes in, but I don't think that'll be too bad.  Also the white plastic, or vinyl, piece in the center.  I also looked at a 2000 Cavalier with a similar knob, but I don't like it as much.  I also looked at the 'Vette one, and that one's a lot better!  I think I don't like the Cavalier one because it's plastic.  The leather one is the way to go.  I saw that Mid America Designs sells the Corvette auto shifter knob, a leather one, for $40.  I don't want to pay this much, but there's no 'Vettes here in auto salvage.  I don't know.  I'm going to look at the shifter assembly tomorrow; I'll see what I'll need to do.  Thanks for the help.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
